{"availability":"available","full":"yochaiye/LipVoicer","name":"LipVoicer","description":"Official Code implementation for the ICLR paper \"LipVoicer: Generating Speech from Silent Videos Guided by Lip Reading\"","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":90,"forks":13,"created":"2023-07-28T13:20:39Z","updated":"2024-09-19T13:28:08Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["diffusion-models","lip-to-speech"],"demo":"https://lipvoicer.github.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:15.267Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:15.267Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:15.267Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:30:31.975Z","stars":89,"forks":13},{"at":"2026-10-10T06:59:46.011Z","stars":89,"forks":13},{"at":"2026-10-15T21:43:59.756Z","stars":90,"forks":13},{"at":"2026-10-19T22:19:15.267Z","stars":90,"forks":13}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Paper | Demo Page | Introduction | Test Files | Pretrained Models | Inference | Training","Official implementation of LipVoicer, a lip-to-speech method. Given a silent video, we first predict the spoken text using a pre-trained lip-reading network. We then condition a diffusion model on the video and use the extracted text through a classifier-guidance mechanism where a pre-trained ASR serves as the classifier. LipVoicer outperforms multiple lip-to-speech baselines on LRS2 and LRS3, which are in-the-wild datasets with hundreds of unique speakers in their test set and an unrestricted vocabulary.","The lip reading network used in LipVoicer is taken from the Visual Speech Recognition for Multiple Languages repository. The ASR system is adapted from Audio-Visual Efficient Conformer for Robust Speech Recognition."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yochaiye/LipVoicer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"866f98eff99f839fbec7483dc68df1fbc2c15d3c053d92c8cc75ff30ac8cabc2","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:32.113Z"},"overvi